# @react-pdf/renderer — PDF Generation Rules

## Package Distinction
- `@react-pdf/renderer` = **creates** PDFs from React components (this project)
- `react-pdf` (wojtekmaj) = **displays** existing PDFs with PDF.js (used for live preview)
- Never confuse them — they have different APIs, different imports, different purposes

## Component Hierarchy

```
<Document>           ← Root: metadata (title, author, subject, keywords)
  <Page>             ← size="A4" | "LETTER" | {width, height}
    <View>           ← Container (like div). Flexbox only — no CSS Grid
      <Text>         ← All text MUST be inside <Text>. Supports nesting for inline styles
      <Image>        ← JPG, PNG, base64. Use cache={true} for remote images
      <Link>         ← Hyperlinks (external URLs or internal anchors)
      <Svg>          ← Vector graphics: <Circle>, <Rect>, <Path>, <Line>, <G>
      <Canvas>       ← Freeform drawing with pdfkit methods
    </View>
  </Page>
</Document>
```

### Critical Component Rules
- **All raw text MUST be wrapped in `<Text>`** — bare strings inside `<View>` cause layout crashes
- **No `<div>`, `<span>`, `<p>`, or HTML elements** — only react-pdf primitives
- **No CSS Grid** — only Flexbox is supported
- **No `display: inline` or `display: block`** — use `flexDirection: "row"` for inline-like layouts
- **SVG numeric values must be numbers, not strings** — `x={10}` not `x="10"` inside render props

## StyleSheet System

Always use `StyleSheet.create()` — it caches styles and improves performance:

```tsx
const styles = StyleSheet.create({
  page: {
    padding: 30,
    fontFamily: "Roboto",
    fontSize: 11,
    color: "#333333",
  },
  section: {
    marginBottom: 10,
    flexDirection: "column",
  },
  row: {
    flexDirection: "row",
    justifyContent: "space-between",
    alignItems: "center",
  },
});
```

### Supported CSS Properties
- **Flexbox**: flexDirection, justifyContent, alignItems, alignSelf, flex, flexWrap, flexGrow, flexShrink, flexBasis, gap, rowGap, columnGap
- **Sizing**: width, height, minWidth, minHeight, maxWidth, maxHeight
- **Spacing**: margin, marginHorizontal, marginVertical, padding, paddingHorizontal, paddingVertical (and all directional variants)
- **Typography**: fontSize, fontFamily, fontStyle, fontWeight, letterSpacing, lineHeight, textAlign, textDecoration, textTransform, textOverflow, maxLines, textIndent
- **Visual**: backgroundColor, color, opacity, border (all variants), borderRadius (all corners)
- **Position**: position ("absolute" | "relative"), top, right, bottom, left, zIndex
- **Media queries**: query based on width, height, orientation of the document

### Properties NOT Supported
- `display: grid`, `display: inline`, `display: block`
- `float`, `clear`
- CSS variables (`var(--x)`)
- `transform`, `transition`, `animation`
- `box-shadow`, `text-shadow`
- `overflow: scroll`

## Font Registration

```tsx
import { Font } from "@react-pdf/renderer";

Font.register({
  family: "Roboto",
  fonts: [
    { src: "/fonts/Roboto-Regular.ttf", fontWeight: 400 },
    { src: "/fonts/Roboto-Medium.ttf", fontWeight: 500 },
    { src: "/fonts/Roboto-Bold.ttf", fontWeight: 700 },
    { src: "/fonts/Roboto-Italic.ttf", fontWeight: 400, fontStyle: "italic" },
    { src: "/fonts/Roboto-BoldItalic.ttf", fontWeight: 700, fontStyle: "italic" },
  ],
});

Font.registerHyphenationCallback((word) => [word]);
```

### Font Rules
- **Only TTF and WOFF** are supported — no OTF, no WOFF2, no variable fonts
- **Always use numeric fontWeight** (400, 700) — string values ("normal", "bold") can cause resolution errors
- **Always call `Font.registerHyphenationCallback((word) => [word])`** to prevent crashes with custom fonts
- **Store fonts in `/public/fonts/`** for Vite/Next.js — import or use public path, not node_modules
- **Register fonts once** at module level, outside components — not inside render functions
- **In Next.js server components**: use `process.cwd() + "/public/fonts/..."` for absolute paths

## Page Breaks and Wrapping

```tsx
<View break />                                    // Force page break before this view
<View wrap={false}>                                // Keep entire view on one page
  <Text>This content stays together</Text>
</View>
<Text orphans={2} widows={2}>Long text...</Text>   // Orphan/widow control
<View minPresenceAhead={100}>                      // Require 100pt of space ahead
  <Text>Content needs space below</Text>
</View>
```

## Fixed Headers and Footers

```tsx
<Page size="A4" style={{ padding: 30, paddingTop: 60, paddingBottom: 50 }}>
  <View fixed style={{ position: "absolute", top: 20, left: 30, right: 30 }}>
    <Text style={{ fontSize: 8, color: "#999" }}>Resume — John Doe</Text>
  </View>

  {/* Main content with margins to avoid overlap */}
  <View style={{ flex: 1 }}>
    <Text>Page content here</Text>
  </View>

  <Text
    fixed
    style={{ position: "absolute", bottom: 20, left: 30, right: 30, textAlign: "center", fontSize: 8 }}
    render={({ pageNumber, totalPages }) => `${pageNumber} / ${totalPages}`}
  />
</Page>
```

## Dynamic Content and Render Props

The `render` prop on `<Text>` and `<View>` provides page context:

```tsx
<Text render={({ pageNumber, totalPages }) => `Page ${pageNumber} of ${totalPages}`} />
```

**Warning**: `render` executes twice — once during layout, once after page count is known. Do not put expensive operations in render props.

## Conditional Rendering

```tsx
// CORRECT — force boolean conversion to avoid empty string nodes
{!!name && <Text>{name}</Text>}
{items.length > 0 && <View>...</View>}

// WRONG — empty string "" is falsy but still creates a node that crashes layout
{name && <Text>{name}</Text>}
```

Always use `!!variable` or explicit comparison (`variable !== ""`) in conditional rendering to prevent the empty-string layout crash.

## Template Pattern for Resumes

Structure reusable PDF components as pure functions:

```tsx
// src/templates/components/SectionHeader.tsx
import { Text, View, StyleSheet } from "@react-pdf/renderer";

const styles = StyleSheet.create({
  container: { marginBottom: 8, borderBottomWidth: 1, borderBottomColor: "#2563eb", paddingBottom: 4 },
  title: { fontSize: 14, fontWeight: 700, color: "#1e293b", textTransform: "uppercase" },
});

interface SectionHeaderProps {
  title: string;
}

export function SectionHeader({ title }: SectionHeaderProps) {
  return (
    <View style={styles.container}>
      <Text style={styles.title}>{title}</Text>
    </View>
  );
}
```

### Template Architecture
- Keep template components in `src/templates/` as pure React components
- Each template is a function: `(resumeData: ResumeData) => JSX.Element` (returns a `<Document>`)
- Share common sub-components (SectionHeader, BulletList, SkillBadge) across templates
- Define theme tokens (colors, spacing, fontSizes) as a config object, not hardcoded
- Never put side effects or hooks in PDF template components

## Performance

- **Use `StyleSheet.create()`** — plain objects skip caching
- **Compress images** before embedding — large images bloat the PDF
- **Use `cache={true}`** on `<Image>` for remote sources
- **Use `renderToStream()`** on the server for large documents instead of `renderToBuffer()`
- **Debounce updates** when using `usePDF()` — rapid re-renders create memory pressure; revoke old blob URLs with `URL.revokeObjectURL()` in cleanup
- **Subset fonts** — use only the weights/styles you need; full font families add hundreds of KB

## Live Preview Architecture

For the editor live preview, use the double-buffer pattern:
1. `usePDF()` generates a blob URL from the `<Document>` component
2. Pass that blob URL to `react-pdf` (wojtekmaj) `<Document file={url}>` for canvas rendering
3. Use a `currentUrlRef` token to prevent stale renders from overwriting newer ones
4. Always `URL.revokeObjectURL(oldUrl)` in the useEffect cleanup to prevent memory leaks
5. Debounce document updates (300-500ms) to avoid excessive re-renders

## Debugging
- Use `debug={true}` on any component to visualize its bounding box
- Check the console for font loading errors — they're often silent failures
- Test page breaks with realistic content lengths — layout behaves differently than web CSS
